{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T17:22:36.012Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"34569ddecaea7f35ebc61713","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"After a release, CI's changelog:check reports 'Changelog is out of date': the generated file has 'No changes.' sections for empty tags that the committed file lacks."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T17:22:36.012Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The release step 'Generate changelog and release notes' expands a shared common=(...) array that lacked --include-empty, while changelog:full (the command CI's changelog:check runs) passes it. The release's own paired --check expands the same array, so it passed and the release committed a CHANGELOG.md without the empty tag sections. CI's changelog:check then refused that file on main and on every following PR. release:check does not run changelog:check in this repo. Correction: the first version of this item said it did; CodeRabbit (PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs61zYYQ) and Greptile (PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs61yPV-) pointed out the right check."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The release commits a CHANGELOG.md without --include-empty, so CI's changelog:check fails on main after every release"}],"before_hash":"e813a0d317e3fbbdacb00dbba6e99cc0d8a79f118a2e5c77a4aafa143bf9d462","after_hash":"f6634ad7bc8c75bb574a6a7159009225c318dc990a5a04220df4b5de1ae92391","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"64cb2134612398e52ee8895c4a68e989540cba55f9fa4c871f8f093a4255743b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T17:22:36.702Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"34569ddecaea7f35ebc61713","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:22:36.701Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"Review round: (1) the attribution in the title, description and test comment is corrected: CI's changelog:check, not release:check. (2) extractCommonArray skips full-line and trailing shell comments, and a new test fails without that (0/1) and passes with it. (3) CHANGELOG.md is regenerated: main's toolchain entry lacked the (#219) link, which the squash merge added after the branch-side regeneration. release-workflow-sync 3/0, typecheck clean."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T17:22:36.702Z"}],"before_hash":"f6634ad7bc8c75bb574a6a7159009225c318dc990a5a04220df4b5de1ae92391","after_hash":"33670e48756165a489147d8bd96f40936d32057121adfcfa22dbccc9032a7091","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0dcabd8409514eb1660bd5bc44815416c6dc1feb261a0a2bd9957033f465584a"}
